# Every text file keeps Linux (LF) line endings on every OS, including Windows checkouts.
# Why: shell scripts run inside Linux containers ("can't execute 'sh'", exit 127 with CRLF),
# and DVC fingerprints code files, so CRLF copies look "modified" in `dvc status`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Data files are left byte-for-byte as committed.
*.csv -text